### What did I learn this week?

This week in English, I practiced annotating a paper. I learned that annotation is very important because it helps me understand the text better. By highlighting key words and writing notes, I can find hidden meanings that I might not notice when reading normally.

### What was challenging?

The challenging part was finding the deeper meaning behind certain words and sentences. Sometimes the meaning is not directly written in the text, so I have to think more carefully.

### What changed my thinking?

Before, I thought annotation was just highlighting important information. Now, I understand that it helps me discover hidden meanings and understand what the writer is trying to tell the reader.

### What do I want to improve?

I want to get better at finding hidden meanings and explaining why the writer uses certain words. I also want to make my annotations more useful instead of just highlighting everything.
